# Tier 1: packed-u64 bit-packing + NEON SIMD, a permutation-invariant
# weight-histogram thermometer pre-filter, and a 64-bit feature-vector
# signature pre-filter for OutputSetIndex.
#
# Applies on top of, in order:
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-macos-proc.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-instrumentation-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-online-subsumption-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-perf-v3.patch
# against the pinned upstream commit 0b5d09c47446096f9e3a0812b35afc72b7f2a718.
# Apply with:  patch -V none -p1 -i <this file>
#
# The Isabelle/HOL-extracted checker (checker/) is not touched.
#
# Three changes, all exact (they only ever skip work that provably cannot
# succeed; no answer changes):
#
#  1. src/output_set/packed.rs (new) - PackedSet, a bit-packed u64 mirror of
#     OutputSet's dense byte-per-Boolean-vector bitmap (bit i in word i>>6,
#     bit position i&63; the same layout as pack_into_slice on little-endian).
#     Provides subsumes_unpermuted (explicit aarch64 NEON with a portable
#     scalar fallback), swap_channels (in-word delta swap / word-pair blend /
#     word permutation, by case), invert (reverse_bits), weight_histogram and
#     low_channels_channel_abstraction (masked popcounts driven by a cached
#     AbstractionTables). src/output_set/subsume.rs - the exact permuted-
#     subsumption solver, ~78 % of active thread time under M2b - now holds
#     PackedSet instead of OutputSet<Vec<bool>>, so its leaf test, its
#     swap_channels and its per-node abstraction all run on u64 words, and it
#     performs no heap allocation at all. src/output_set/index.rs no longer
#     unpacks a candidate to 2^k bools before testing it: it goes straight
#     from the stored packed bytes to a PackedSet by memcpy.
#
#  2. The weight-histogram thermometer. A channel permutation permutes cube
#     coordinates and so preserves Hamming weight; complementation maps weight
#     w to k-w. Hence "exists pi: pi(A) subset-of B" requires
#     hist_A[w] <= hist_B[w] for all w, and "exists pi: pi(complement(A))
#     subset-of B" requires hist_A[k-w] <= hist_B[w] for all w. Both polarities
#     are tested separately and each gates only its own branch of
#     LowerInvert::test_precise, so the filter is one-sided in the safe
#     direction. Applied everywhere subsumes_permuted is reached: the on-line
#     index, prune and gen-proof.
#
#  3. A 64-bit invariant signature per stored index entry (E-prover/SatELite
#     lineage): 5 monotone thermometer bits per Hamming weight, bit j of slot w
#     set iff hist[w] >= ceil(binomial(k,w)*(j+1)/6). Monotone thresholds give
#     the containment property hist_A <= hist_B implies sig_A & !sig_B == 0, so
#     sig_A & !sig_B != 0 is a sound one-instruction reject, evaluated before
#     the abstraction test and before any unpacking. Tree nodes carry the AND
#     and the OR of their subtree's signatures (Augmentation::sig_and/sig_or),
#     which reject whole subtrees in the lookup and eviction directions
#     respectively.
#
# Env gates (all default ON, off only for "0"/"false"/"no"):
#   SORTNETOPT_TIER1_SIG    - the signature pre-filter (change 3)
#   SORTNETOPT_TIER1_HIST   - the histogram pre-filter (change 2)
#   SORTNETOPT_FILTER_AUDIT - run the exact test on every pair a filter
#                             rejected and panic on disagreement (validation)
#
